{# Visitor count, from GoatCounter's JSON counter endpoint.

   Deliberately NOT GoatCounter's <img>/iframe badge: this fetches
   `https://CODE.goatcounter.com/counter/<path>.json` and writes the number into our
   own markup, so there is no GoatCounter branding, no fixed 200x80 box, and the
   number inherits the theme's type and color like any other pill.

   TWO switches must both be on for a number to appear, and the second one is not
   ours:
     1. `show_visitor_count: true` in the vault's _bloob-settings.md (default off)
     2. "Allow using the visitor counter" in the GoatCounter site's own settings
        (ALSO default off — without it the endpoint answers 403)
   Failure is silent by design: the element is empty until a count arrives, so a site
   that has only flipped switch 1 shows nothing rather than an error.

   Per-page override wins over the site setting: `visitor_count: false` in a note's
   frontmatter hides it on that page; `visitor_count: true` shows it even when the
   site default is off.

   The site code is derived from the goat-counter-tracking snippet — see
   parseGoatCounterCode() in scripts/utils/bloob-settings-reader.js. #}

{# `is defined` rather than `!== undefined`: a page that sets `visitor_count: false`
   must still count as having made a choice, and it is the only form that survives a
   site.analytics that predates this feature. #}
{% set vcSite = site.analytics.show_visitor_count if site.analytics else false %}
{% set vcCode = site.analytics.goatcounter_code if site.analytics else null %}
{% set vcOn = visitor_count if visitor_count is defined else vcSite %}

{% if vcCode and vcOn %}
<p class="visitor-count" data-pagefind-ignore hidden
   data-goatcounter-code="{{ vcCode }}">
  <span class="visitor-count__number"></span>
  <span class="visitor-count__label">views</span>
</p>
<script>
(function () {
  var el = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;
  if (!el || !el.classList.contains('visitor-count')) return;
  var code = el.dataset.goatcounterCode;
  // GoatCounter keys pageviews by path, and its counter route expects the path to keep
  // its leading slash — hence the doubled slash in /counter//some/page.json.
  var url = 'https://' + code + '.goatcounter.com/counter/' +
            encodeURIComponent(location.pathname).replace(/%2F/g, '/') + '.json';
  fetch(url)
    .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : null; })
    .then(function (d) {
      if (!d || !d.count) return;           // 403 = counter not enabled in GoatCounter
      el.querySelector('.visitor-count__number').textContent = d.count;
      el.removeAttribute('hidden');
    })
    .catch(function () { /* offline or blocked — stay hidden */ });
})();
</script>
{% endif %}
